== 4. CRITICAL DECRYPTION: YUKA AND NUTRI-SCORE VS. WHOLE SCRATCH COOKING
<critical-decryption-yuka-and-nutri-score-vs-whole-scratch-cooking>
=== A. Yuka: Citizen Feat and Algorithmic Biases
<a.-yuka-citizen-feat-and-algorithmic-biases>
The Yuka smartphone scanning app represents a citizen triumph in forcing food corporations toward label transparency. However, its scoring algorithm exhibits inherent technical biases:
- It scores packaged foods out of 100 based on Nutri-Score (60%), additives (30%), and organic certification (10%).
- While remarkably effective at red-flagging toxic preservatives and endocrine disruptors, it still operates within the boundaries of industrial packaged goods, occasionally penalizing whole single-ingredient ancestral fats (such as pure duck fat or virgin olive oil).

=== B. Nutri-Score: The Blindness to Ultra-Processing
<b.-nutri-score-the-blindness-to-ultra-processing>
The governmental Nutri-Score logo calculates an abstract mathematical balance per #strong[100 grams of food], offsetting unfavorable nutrients (calories, simple sugars, saturated fats, sodium) against favorable components (fiber, protein, fruit/vegetable percentage).

$ upright("Nutri-Score Points") = upright("Unfavorable Points") - upright("Favorable Points") $

- #strong[Fatal Blindness to Cracking and Extrusion:] Nutri-Score completely ignores the NOVA degree of ultra-processing. A box of industrialized children's breakfast cereal—formulated from high-pressure hydrolyzed cornstarch, artificial aromas, and emulsifiers—captures a triumphant #strong[Nutri-Score A] simply because the manufacturer fortified it with isolated oat fibers and soy protein isolates!
- #strong[Unfair Penalty on Heritage Treasures:] Ancestral single-ingredient fermented foods—raw milk Roquefort, dry mountain ham, canned sardines in olive oil—are branded with punitive D or E scores, while artificially sweetened, nutrient-stripped diet sodas earn a B or C.

#chef_tip[
==== 💡 The Single-Ingredient Manifesto: The Infallible Rule
<the-single-ingredient-manifesto-the-infallible-rule>
To nourish your body and household sustainably, there exists a sovereign guideline that outclasses every silicon algorithm and official sticker: #strong[buy ingredients that have no ingredient list].
- A fresh bunch of carrots with greens, a whole wild mackerel, a bag of dried green lentils, and a glass bottle of extra-virgin olive oil have no E-numbers, no Nutri-Score, and no chemical stabilizers.
- When you cook starting from raw matter with the minimal tools of Chapter 04, the additive question dissolves entirely: you control 100% of the molecules that enter your skillet.
]

