==== 1. The Black Garbage Bag (Landfill Disaster)
When organic scraps (70% to 80% water) are sealed inside plastic garbage bags and compacted in anaerobic landfills, they ferment putridly, releasing #strong[methane ($upright("CH")_4$)], a greenhouse gas with a global warming potential #strong[28 times higher than $upright("CO")_2$], while generating toxic acidic leachate that contaminates groundwater tables.

==== 2. The Green Bin (Compost and Biomethanation: The Living Cycle)
- #strong[Horticultural Composting:] Aerobic bacteria and earthworms transform cellulose into stable, nitrogen-rich organic humus that restores soil water retention without chemical fertilizers.
- #strong[Biomethanation:] Organic waste digested in heated anaerobic digesters produces biomethane injected into municipal gas grids to heat homes, while the nutrient-rich digestate fertilizes farmland.

#chef_tip[
==== 💡 The Zero-Waste Chef's Reflex
<the-zero-waste-chefs-reflex>
Never discard a roasted chicken carcass. Simmering bones with a splash of cider vinegar (whose mild acid extracts bone minerals and collagen) yields golden, gelatinous poultry stock worthy of a three-star restaurant.
]

